  "rationale": "structural: The requirement says the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct an agent that cannot ask the user to stop, leave the drafts uncommitted, and report the revised drafts and the design questions. Every clause is about what the skill document tells an agent to do. No clause prescribes a library, algorithm, signature, type, field, or delegation through a named interface. Any wording in the skill that gives the same direction would satisfy the text, so the choice of wording is discretionary and no structural obligation needs implementation evidence.\n\nThe root `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` does contain the direction. Workflow step 4, at `section[Habeas%20requirements]/section[Workflow]/paragraph@7b764a629ec4`, says: \"If you cannot ask the user in this session, stop, leave the drafts uncommitted, and report them with the design questions.\" Step 4 comes after the review in which the drafts are revised, so \"them\" refers to the revised drafts. I found nothing missing.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement is one behavioral obligation about the text of the bundled `habeas-requirements` skill. The skill MUST direct an agent that cannot ask the user to (a) stop, (b) leave the drafts uncommitted, and (c) report the drafts and the design questions.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_stops_and_reports_when_it_cannot_ask_the_user]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It calls `assert_phrases` on the `habeas-requirements` skill with the sentence \"If you cannot ask the user in this session, stop, leave the drafts uncommitted, and report them with the design questions\".\n\n`assert_phrases` calls `assert_text` on `bundled_skill(name)`. `bundled_skill` joins `SKILL.md` and its reference files and collapses whitespace. `assert_text` asserts `text.contains(phrase)`, so line wrapping does not affect the match.\n\nThe sentence covers all three parts: the condition (cannot ask the user), stopping, leaving the drafts uncommitted, and reporting the drafts together with the design questions. I read the skill source at `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, in the Workflow section. It contains this directive, so the assertion is meaningful.\n\nA skill that dropped or weakened any of the three parts would fail the `contains` assertion. I found no other obligation or boundary in the text that needs a separate test.",
